SVG
{EMBED HERE}
0.1430.037100011 The invention relates to a method for applying aerodynamically functional film to abody around which complex flow occurs, for example on a commercial aircraft.

SVG
{EMBED HERE}
0.1430.037100021 Aerodynamically functional films are known in different embodiments and areas ofapplication from the prior art, and are generally used to reduce the wall shear stress on surfaces of bodies around which flow occurs. The aerodynamically functional films generally have a microstructured surface having one or more preferred directions for this purpose. A preferred direction refers here to a preferred overflow direction (thus the direction of the local flow on the surface), in which the reduction of the wall shear stress is particularly high or even maximal.

SVG
{EMBED HERE}
0.1430.037100031 One widespread microstructure is the so-called riblet structure, having very small ribsextending essentially along the preferred direction. Riblet structures are thus found, for example, on external surfaces of aircraft, but also on rotor blades of wind turbines, on the outer skin of ships, or on outer surfaces of high-speed trains.

SVG
{EMBED HERE}
0.1430.037100041 In order that the most extensive possible reduction of the wall shear stress can beachieved by aerodynamically functional films and in particular riblet structures, it is necessary that the film is aligned having its preferred direction as exactly as possible in or only with minor deviations in relation to the local flow direction - thus that direction in which the overflow of the surface is primarily to be expected in the region of the film.

SVG
{EMBED HERE}
0.1430.037100061 To reduce the flow resistance of a body around which flow occurs as extensively aspossible, it is desirable in principle also to provide aerodynamically functional films reducing the wall shear stress on those surfaces of the body in which a more complex flow profile is present.

[0032]   It is preferred if the predetermined angle range is ±70 or less, preferably  SVG
{EMBED HERE}
0.1130.23 or less,more preferably +30 or less. Corresponding angle ranges often provide a good compromise between the size of the fields which can be located and the effectiveness of the film, thus in particular the reduction of the wall stress, in the majority of possible aerodynamically functional films.
